@startuml reboot-restore
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

' After a reboot (or at any login, or by hand): the login agent runs
' keeper up, the single entry point that brings the node back. The session
' host starts, the main loop's session resumes, each owned process's root
' orchestrator resumes from its goal and park note, queued doorbells are
' delivered, and the main loop reports to the person. Sub-orchestrators and
' runs are left to each root orchestrator.
' Sources: main loop spec DRAFT v0.1 §1.1, §7.3, §10.5, §10.6.

title Reboot: keeper up restores the node
caption Sources: main loop DRAFT v0.1 §1.1, §7.3, §10.5, §10.6

skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor $SERVICE
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor $SERVICE_LINE

participant "Login agent\n(launchd or systemd,\nuser level)" as agent
participant "keeper up" as up
participant "Session host" as host
participant "Main loop session" as loop $AGENT
participant "Calendar root orchestrator" as cal $AGENT
participant "Café root orchestrator" as cafe $AGENT
database "Boards\n(goals, park notes)" as boards $COMMITTED
actor "Person" as person $PERSON

== Login ==
agent -> up : run at login (idempotent)
up -> host : start
host -> host : read the session registry

== The main loop ==
up -> host : resume the main loop's session
alt the harness session still exists
  host -> loop : native resume
else it is gone
  host -> boards : read the main loop's goal and park note
  host -> loop : new session, goal injected\nwith the park note
end

== Each owned process, in registry order ==
up -> host : resume each owned process's root orchestrator\n(not those the person stopped)
host -> boards : goal and park note of the calendar
host -> cal : resume natively, or new session\nwith goal and park note
host -> boards : goal and park note of the café
host -> cafe : resume natively, or new session\nwith goal and park note
note over cal, cafe
  Each reads its park note and board obligations first,
  then decides which sub-orchestrators and runs to restart.
  keeper up restarts none of them.
end note

== Afterwards ==
host -> cal : deliver queued doorbells
host -> cafe : deliver queued doorbells
loop -> person : report: what came back, what did not and why\n(terminal or channel)

@enduml
